details:
(a) the Foreign Portfolio Investor (FPI) outflows from Indian equity markets during 2025 and the outflows recorded in 2026 till date month-wise;
(b) whether 2025 witnessed one of the highest ever FPI equity sell-offs and the total value of equity outflows during the year;
(c) the corresponding movement and percentage decline in major indices such as Sensex, NIFTY-50 and NIFTY-500 during months of heavy FPI selling;
(d) whether the decline in foreign holdings indicates weak global confidence in India’s equity markets; and
(e) the key reasons identified for continued FPI withdrawals, including global interest rates, geopolitical risks and domestic policy factors?

(a) the stretch-wise Water Quality Index of the river Yamuna during the last five years, including the current year;
(b) the year-wise levels of Biochemical Oxygen Demand Dissolved Oxygen and faecal coliform at major monitoring stations;
(c) whether it is a fact that BOD levels remain 8–10 times above prescribed standards and faecal coliform levels far exceed permissible limits;
(d) whether Government acknowledges that Yamuna water quality has shown limited improvement despite successive action plans; and
(e) the year-wise details of funds allocated, released and utilised over the last five years for Yamuna pollution abatement under Namami Gange Programme and other schemes?

(a) whether it is a fact that vegetable farmers in Assam are facing significant losses due to inadequate cold storage facilities and dependence on middlemen;
(b) the number, location and operational status of cold storage units established in Assam by Government and private sector in the State;
(c) whether Government is aware of the large price gap between farm-gate rates and urban market prices for vegetables such as potatoes, cauliflowers, green peas and tomatoes; and
(d) whether Government has considered implementing alternative mechanisms, including mini cold storages, direct procurement or market linkages, to protect farmers from distress sales?

(a) whether Government has estimated the time required to fill all sanctioned vacancies of Vice-Chancellors, Registrars, teaching and non-teaching staff in Central Universities, IITs, NITs, IIMs and other Central Higher Educational Institutions;
(b) whether any time-bound roadmap or deadline has been fixed to achieve 100 per cent filling of sanctioned posts, if so, the details thereof;
(c) if no such timeline exists, the reasons for the continued absence of a definite recruitment schedule despite large-scale and long-pending vacancies; and
(d) whether Government acknowledges that the lack of a clear timeline has prolonged administrative paralysis and academic disruption in several institutions?

(a) whether it is a fact that the qualifying cut-off marks for postgraduate medical admissions were drastically reduced in 2025;
(b) whether Government acknowledges that such reductions have made candidates with extremely low or even negative scores eligible for counselling, raising concerns over academic standards and merit in postgraduate medical education;
(c) whether the primary reason for reducing cut-offs was the failure to fill over 18,000 PG medical seats even after multiple rounds of counselling; and
(d) whether Government has assessed the risk of compromising the quality of specialist training and patient safety by admitting candidates with very low performance scores?

(a) whether Government has introduced or approved any special restrictions or differentiated procedures for Aadhaar enrollment in Assam, particularly for first-time applicants above the age of eighteen years;
(b) if so, the rationale and legal basis for restricting or deferring Aadhaar issuance to adults in Assam and the categories of persons exempted from such restrictions;
(c) whether it is a fact that Aadhaar saturation in Assam has reportedly exceeded 100 percent, if so, the details thereof, district-wise; and
(d) whether such over-saturation or data anomalies have been examined to identify duplication, irregular enrolments or projection errors , if so, the findings thereof?

(a) the policy changes undertaken during the last five years in relation to investment, trade, visas and economic engagement with China, including measures adopted after the Galwan incident and the issuance of Press Note 3 (2020);
(b) whether Government is pursuing any graded or conditional easing of restrictions on Chinese investments, business visas or skilled labour and if so, the details thereof; and
(c) whether any such relaxation is being contemplated subject to reciprocal measures by China and the criteria adopted to define and enforce the principle of reciprocity?

(a) the number of complaints received by the National Commission for Women (NCW) from Manipur since May, 2023, particularly relating to rape, sexual violence, trafficking, displacement and other crimes against women;
(b) the nature of action taken by the NCW in each category of cases, including fact-finding visits, recommendations, coordination with State authorities, police and courts;
(c) whether the NCW provided any legal aid, counselling, medical assistance, rehabilitation support or compensation facilitation to women survivors, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the number of cases in which justice has been secured, including FIR registration, arrests, charge-sheets or convictions, following NCW intervention?

(a) whether Government has taken note of findings indicating that over two-thirds of children aged 6–59 months in the country are anaemic, according to the National Indicator Framework Progress Report 2025;
(b) whether Government has assessed the trend in childhood anaemia levels during the last five years, and the factors contributing to the worsening situation despite implementation of multiple nutrition and health programmes;
(c) whether the existing nutrition and supplementation schemes have been evaluated for their effectiveness in reducing anaemia among children; and
(d) the measures currently being implemented to prevent, detect and treat childhood anaemia, particularly among vulnerable groups?

(a) whether Government has taken note of reports indicating a record surge in sales of respiratory medicines, crossing ?1,950 crore in December 2025, with sustained year-on-year increases during high-pollution months;
(b) whether Government acknowledges that such sharp increases in sales of anti-asthma, Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD) and allergy medications reflect a worsening air-pollution-linked public health burden rather than mere seasonal illness;
(c) whether any official study or epidemiological assessment has been conducted to establish a direct correlation between air pollution levels and rising respiratory morbidity and deaths; and
(d) the number of pollution-related respiratory illnesses and deaths reported annually during the last five years, State-wise?

(a) the total funds allocated, released and utilised in Guwahati under Smart City Mission during the last three years, year-wise;
(b) the component-wise break-up of funds, including expenditure on roads, drainage, water supply, solid waste management, housing, ICT and other sectors;
(c) the total funds allocated and utilised specifically for drainage under the Mission;
(d) the number of drainage and flood-mitigation projects sanctioned and completed/ongoing in Guwahati, along with their present status; and
(e) whether any proposal has been approved or is under consideration for inclusion of Silchar under Smart City-related flood mitigation project/programme?

(a) number and details of airports, heliports and water aerodromes proposed in the State of Assam under the UDAN (Ude Desh ka Aam Naagrik) scheme since its inception;
(b) current status of each such project, indicating the number and details that have been completed, partially completed or remain under construction;
(c) number of airports, heliports and water aerodromes in Assam that are operational, non-operational or where flight services have been discontinued, along with reasons thereof;
(d) duration for which flight operations were conducted before discontinuation, wherever applicable; and
(e) total funds allocated, released and utilised for UDAN projects in Assam, infrastructure-wise and year-wise?

(a) the current status of airports proposal at Karbi Anglong and Doloo (Cachar) in the State of Assam, and whether they are at the concept, feasibility, approval, or implementation stage;
(b) whether any feasibility study, site survey, or techno-economic assessment has been conducted for these proposed airports, and the findings thereof;
(c) whether the proposals have been examined under any the Central scheme, including UDAN or other regional connectivity initiatives;
(d) whether any land acquisition, environmental clearance, or inter-ministerial consultation issues are pending, and the details thereof; and
(e) whether any timeline has been fixed for approval and commencement of construction of these airports?
V

(a) the total number of tea gardens and workers employed, administered or managed by Public Sector Undertakings (PSUs) in Assam and other North-Eastern States, PSU-wise and State-wise;
(b) whether there are any pending or unpaid wages, arrears or statutory dues to workers in these tea gardens and the amount pending, State-wise;
(c) whether Government has taken cognisance of delays or irregularities in wage payments in PSU-managed tea gardens and the action taken thereon; and
(d) whether there exists any disparity in wages, benefits or working conditions between workers employed in PSU-administered tea gardens and privately owned tea gardens, if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government is aware of the announcement by the United States imposing or proposing a 25 percent tariff on countries continuing trade with Iran;
(b) the quantity and value of tea and rice exported by India to Iran since 2020, year-wise;
(c) the estimated share of such exports that may be affected due to the said US tariff measures, particularly for tea growers, rice exporters and MSMEs; and
(d) whether Government has assessed the potential loss to Indian exporters arising from reduced access to the US market or increased trade barriers linked to Iran-related transactions?

(a) whether Government has examined the impact of subsuming the Working Journalists Act, 1955 and the Working Journalists (Fixation of Rates of Wages) Act, 1958 under the Occupational Safety, Health and Working Conditions Code, 2020 on the service conditions of working journalists;
(b) whether it is a fact that the new Labour Codes do not retain any journalist-specific protections relating to wages, working hours, leave, night work, retrenchment compensation, gratuity or conditions of service; and
(c) whether Government acknowledges concerns that the new framework places working journalists under general labour laws, thereby reversing long-standing sector-specific protections?

(a) whether it is a fact that incidents of human–animal conflict have increased in Assam since 2021;
(b) the number of human and wild animals deaths and injuries caused due to human–animal conflict in the State since 2021, year-wise and species-wise;
(c) whether Government has assessed changes in forest cover, wildlife habitat size and corridor connectivity in the State since 2021 and if so, the details thereof; and
(d) whether habitat fragmentation, encroachment, linear infrastructure and land-use change have contributed to increased conflict in the State?

(a) whether the forthcoming census is proposed to be conducted using digital modes, including mobile applications for enumerators and provisions for online self-enumeration by households;
(b) the details of the data-collection architecture envisaged, including the use of mobile apps, online portals, data security safeguards and the availability of offline or paper-based enumeration alternatives;
(c) whether Government has assessed levels of digital illiteracy, internet inaccessibility and device unavailability among rural, tribal, elderly and economically weaker populations; and
(d) whether specific measures have been undertaken to prevent the exclusion of digitally disconnected or illiterate groups from the census, and if so, the details thereof?

(a) the total number of Nipah virus cases reported in the country since its first detection, along with the number of deaths, year-wise and State-wise;
(b) whether Government has assessed the fatality rate and transmission patterns in recent outbreaks;
(c) the measures taken by the Central Government to prevent, detect and contain Nipah virus outbreaks, including surveillance, testing, isolation and contact tracing;
(d) whether any advisories, standard operating procedures or guidelines have been issued to State Governments and health authorities in this regard and the details thereof; and
(e) the technical, financial and logistical support provided by the Centre to vulnerable States?

(a) whether Government is aware that the International Monetary Fund (IMF) has assigned a low (C-grade) data quality rating to India’s GDP estimates;
(b) whether Government acknowledges concerns raised by economists and international agencies regarding the reliability and transparency of India’s GDP data;
(c) the reason as to why GDP estimates continue to be based on the 2011–12 base year, despite significant changes in consumption patterns, employment structure, etc, over the last decade;
(d) whether Government has examined structural mismatch between headline GDP growth figures and ground-level indicators; and
(e) whether Government provides GDP and macroeconomic data directly to international organisations such as IMF and World Bank?

(a) whether it is a fact that funds under the Jal Jeevan Mission (JJM) for FY 2025–26 have been reduced, or delayed for the State of Assam, if so, the amount involved;
(b) the reasons for delaying funds to Assam under the Mission, including issues related to utilisation, reporting, quality of works, or audit observations for FY 2025-26;
(c) whether Government has taken cognisance of irregularities in the implementation of the JJM at the national level reported by media; and
(d) whether any penalties, recoveries, blacklisting of contractors, or disciplinary action against officials have been initiated in Assam, and the details thereof?

(a) the details of the funds allocated, released and expended by Assam under the Deendayal Antyodaya Yojana-National Rural Livelihood Mission (DAY-NRLM) during the last five years;
(b) the number of Institutions of the Poor (IoP) recognised in Assam under the DAY-NRLM, district-wise;
(c) the details and the number of IoPs that specifically cater to female tribal population in Assam, year-wise; and
(d) the number of individuals who have been trained under the DAY-NRLM’s Aajeevika Skills Development Programme in Assam during the said period?

(a) whether Government has formulated a national strategy to address regional disparities and infrastructural deficiencies in youth development and sports in Assam;
(b) the number of Khelo India Centres of Excellence, Sports Science Centres and Talent Identification Hubs established in the State;
(c) the initiatives taken to encourage youth leadership and increase sports participation among women, differently-abled youth and those from socio-economically backward districts of the State; and
(d) the specific measures or programmes implemented to promote youth development and sports in districts with unique challenges, such as Barak Valley and the Northeastern hill areas of the State?

(a) the details and the number of Tribal research and training institutes currently functional in the North-East, State-wise;
(b) the amount of funds allocated to the Tribal research and training institutes in North-East during the last five years;
(c) the details of heads under which the said funds have been utilised; and
(d) the status of utilisation of the remaining funds by the said institute?

(a) whether the Ministry is aware of the sale of medicines including cough syrups in the country without prescription;
(b) if so, whether the Ministry has taken any step in this regard and if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether there is any proposal for laws and regulations regarding restrictions on the sale of over-the-counter cough syrups; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) total funds allocated, released and utilised for Urban Local Bodies (ULBs) in Assam under various central schemes since 2020, year-wise and ULB-wise;
(b) whether Government has provided any special financial assistance, performance-based grants or supplementary allocations to specific cities or towns in the State of Assam during the above period and if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether any ULBs in Assam have reported delays in receiving central funds or faced reductions in allocations, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) whether Government has undertaken any assessment of the financial health and revenue-raising capacity of ULBs in Assam, if so, the key findings and recommendations?

(a) the total number of MGNREGA workers in Assam before the introduction of mandatory e-KYC and the number after its implementation;
(b) the total number of workers deleted from the MGNREGA database in Assam due to failure to complete e-KYC, biometric mismatch, Aadhaar authentication errors, or other technical reasons;
(c) whether Government has verified if the workers deleted from the database were genuine job card holders, and if so, details of the verification process undertaken; and 
(d) total number of workers who have been added or re-added to the MGNREGA database in Assam after completing e-KYC since the system was introduced?
SR

(a) the details of the ongoing development projects, along with those running behind schedule, in the Autonomous District Councils of Bodoland, Dima Hasao and Karbi Anglong;
(b) whether a number of projects are delayed due to financial sanctions and discrepancies in fund release; and
(c) if so, the details thereof and the action taken by Government in this regard?

(a) the current status of implementation of wildlife-friendly measures on NH-715 stretch passing through Kaziranga National Park;
(b) the projected timeline for completion of 34.45 km elevated corridor and bypasses to facilitate free and safe movement of wildlife;
(c) the measures in place to monitor and mitigate the adverse impacts of highway widening on habitat connectivity and species mortality; and
(d) whether any independent ecological assessments and local community consultations have been undertaken or planned for this project?

(a) the current status of the Shillong–Silchar Corridor project, including the total length, sections completed and those under construction;
(b) the original and revised timelines for completion of the corridor and the present expected date of completion;
(c) whether Government has conducted any review of the quality of works executed so far, especially in the hilly and landslide-prone stretches; and
(d) the steps being taken to expedite the completion of the remaining sections and ensure all-weather connectivity between Shillong and Silchar at the earliest?

(a) whether Government is aware of the steep rise in domestic airfares, on Silchar–Guwahati route where ticket prices have reportedly surged abnormally during peak travel periods and emergencies, if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether it is a fact that Government has capped airfares on any specific routes in the past to prevent excessive fare hikes;
(c) whether Government has held any consultations with private airlines for capping or regulating airfares during natural disasters, public emergencies or sudden route disruptions; and
(d) whether Government maintains any real-time monitoring system to track and prevent such exploitative fare hikes?

(a) the total number of railway projects sanctioned in the State of Assam during the last five years, along with details of projects specifically sanctioned for the Barak Valley region;
(b) the current status of each of these projects, including those pertaining to new lines, gauge conversion, electrification and doubling works;
(c) the total funds sanctioned, released and utilised so far under each of these projects;
(d) the original and revised timelines fixed for their completion, along with reasons for delay, if any; and
(e) whether Government has taken any steps to expedite completion of pending railway projects in the Barak Valley region, if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has acknowledged the increasing contractualisation of employment across sectors since 2014 and if so, the policy behind promoting this contractualisation;
(b) the share of contractual workers across various sectors, including both public and private sectors;
(c) the share of workforce that has been provided with social security benefits such as provident fund, insurance, etc., year-wise since 2020 till date; and
(d) whether there is average wage difference between permanent and contractual employees in Government and private sectors and if so, the details thereof, year-wise since 2020?

(a) the total number of National Highway and other major road projects sanctioned in the State of Assam, especially Barak Valley region, during the last five years;
(b) the current status of each of these projects, including those relating to widening, strengthening, new construction and maintenance;
(c) the total funds sanctioned, released and utilised so far under each of these projects; and 
(d) the original and revised timelines fixed for completion, along with reasons for delay, if any?
SR

(a) the present operational status of 121 km Long Lakhipur to Bhanga National Waterway-16 in Assam;
(b) the original and revised timelines fixed for making this stretch fully operational and the extent of physical and financial progress achieved so far;
(c) the total funds sanctioned, released and utilised for the development of National Waterway-16, since its inception, year-wise; and 
(d) the steps being taken by Government to expedite the completion and ensure full operationalisation of the Lakhipur to Bhanga stretch for seamless navigation and trade connectivity in the Barak Valley region?

(a) the details of the total works completed and the percentage of rural households provided with Functional Household Tap Connections (FHTC) under the first phase of Jal Jeevan Mission (JJM) in Assam;
(b) the total budgetary allocation (centre-state share) made for the extended period of the JJM and the funds released to Assam during the current financial year;
(c) the details of the remaining works to be completed under the extended phase of JJM in Assam; and 
(d) whether any financial or implementation liabilities have been placed on Assam under the first phase of JJM, if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government is aware of the recent State of AI-Powered Cybercrime: Threat & Mitigation Report 2025, which highlights that ?22,812 crore were lost due to digital frauds in 2024, much of it driven by Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools and techniquess; 
(b) the total number of cybercrime complaints and financial losses due to AI-driven cybercrimes registered across the country in 2024 and how it compares with previous years; and
(c) the specific steps taken by Government to develop and deploy AI-based threat detection and monitoring tools and integrate cybersecurity awareness and digital safety education in schools and workplaces?

(a) the extent of damage caused to life, property, crops and infrastructure in the recent flood in Assam;
(b) the details of funds released to Assam under the State Disaster Response Fund (SDRF) and National Disaster Response Fund (NDRF) during the last five years;
(c) the criteria adopted by Government to classify a disaster as a ‘national disaster’;
(d) whether Government has received any request from Government of Assam to declare the floods a ‘national disaster’, if so, the details thereof; and
(e) whether Government is developing any integrated flood management strategy for the North-Eastern region, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the scheme and programmes operational for supporting the Urban Local Bodies (ULBs) acorss the country;
(b) the total funds allocated and sanctioned to ULBs of Assam during the last five years;
(c) the current guidelines under the Finance Commission for the grants and transfers to ULBs; 
(d) whether Government is considering to change allocation pattern to ULBs under 16th Finance Commission, if so, the details thereof; and 
(e) whether Government has received any representation from the ULBs across the country, if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government is aware of the investigation conducted by a Railway Zone highlighting that loco pilots are being forced to work continuously for 13-14 hours, if so, the details thereof;
(b) the action taken against officials who allegedly coerced loco pilots into falsifying duty records in the Crew Management System (CMS); and
(c) whether Government has compiled division-wise data on violations of maximum permissible working hours for loco pilots, particularly in goods train operations, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the incidents of violence, persecution or systemic discrimination against religious minorities in neighbouring countries in the last five years;
(b) the details of any formal diplomatic communications, protests, or démarches issued by India in response to such incidents;
(c) whether Government has urged these countries to uphold international obligations for the protection of minority communities, in line with the UN Declaration on the Rights of Persons Belonging to National or Ethnic, Religious and Linguistic Minorities (1992), if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the institutional or bilateral mechanisms in place to address issues of minority safety and religious freedom with neighbouring countries?

(a) whether Government has taken any step to review and amend the National Commission for Women Act, 1990, as recommended by the Parliamentary Committee on the Empowerment of Women and various expert bodies, if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether Government is considering measures to enhance the institutional independence, financial autonomy and legal authority of the NCW, if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether Government proposes to make NCW recommendations binding or ensure implementation within a stipulated timeframe, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the steps taken by Government to ensure that the Commission acts independently and impartially?

(a) the total number of suicides and suicide rate per 1,00,000 population reported annually from 2018 to 2022, and the number of suicides linked with mental health issue State-wise;
(b) the current status of the Tele-MANAS (Tele Mental Health Assistance and Networking Across States) programme, including State-wise utilisation, demographic distribution of users, languages offered;
(c) the details of funds allocated and utilised under the National Tele Mental Health Programme (NTMHP) since its inception; and
(d) whether an impact evaluation of the Mental Healthcare Act, 2017 in ensuring accessible, non-discriminatory, and quality mental health care has been conducted, if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether there are significant cost escalations in projects sanctioned under the Jal Jeevan Mission (JJM), if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether Government has changed the tender operational guidelines several times since the inception of JJM, which led to cost escalation, if so, the details thereof;
(c) the total number of projects where the discovered tender cost exceeded the pre-approved estimated cost; 
(d) the total estimated cost versus discovered cost, and total quantum of escalation recorded; and
(e) whether Government has initiated any probe into potential irregularities in tender awarding, contract approvals, or inflated costs, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the number of startups that have shut down from 2022 to 2025 so far;
(b) the number of startups set up and shut down in the North-Eastern region since the inception of Startup India programme, year-wise and State-wise;
(c) the major factors identified by Government for the surge in Startup closures across sectors;
(d) whether Government has conducted or proposes to conduct any sector-wise analysis to understand patterns of cash burn, customer retention challenges and operational inefficiencies in startups, if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the steps being taken to encourage startup consolidation, mergers and acquisitions to protect innovation and employment?

(a) whether Government is aware that India has dropped to 131st position out of 148 countries in the World Economic Forum’s Global Gender Gap Index;
(b) the measures undertaken by Government to improve India’s ranking in the Global Gender Gap Index;
(c) whether Government has assessed the impact of the Beti Bachao Beti Padhao (BBBP) scheme in improving India’s ranking in the Global Gender Gap Index; and
(d) the total funds allocated and utilised under BBBP during the last five years, year-wise, State-wise, and individual component-wise, spent in publicity and advertisements as a separate head?

(a) the details of the recently approved 168 km long Shillong to Silchar highway project;
(b) the estimated cost, expected timeline for completion, land acquisition, and present status of the project, including major engineering challenges due to hilly terrain;
(c) whether this project will be connected to the Kaladan Multi-Modal Transit Transport Project, if so, the details of the timeline for the same;
(d) the projected reduction in travel time and distance between Shillong and Silchar due to this corridor; and
(e) the estimated employment opportunities the project is expected to generate during construction and post-completion phases?

(a) the total amount of revenue collected through various cesses and surcharges, including on health, petrol, diesel, etc., in the last five years, category-wise, year-wise;
(b) whether Government is considering to include them in the divisible pool of taxes shared with the States, as demanded by several State Governments, if so, the details thereof;
(c) the sector-wise and scheme-wise utilisation of funds collected through such cesses and surcharges during the said period; and
(d) whether it is a fact that a large amount of Central Government funds collected through cesses and surcharges since 2019-20 is unutilised, if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has received any proposal from Governments of various North Eastern States regarding the constitution of a Barak Board and other River Boards on the lines of the Brahmaputra Board, if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether Government has provided any financial, technical, or institutional support for development, and river basin management projects in the Barak Valley region, if so, the details thereof; and
(c) steps taken by Government to ensure equitable water resource planning and disaster mitigation in the various river basins of Northeast, in view of its distinct hydrological challenges compared to the Brahmaputra basin?

(a) whether Government has taken cognisance of the recent remark by the Chief Advisor of Bangladesh regarding the North-eastern States as ‘landlocked’ during his visit to China, if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether these remarks were officially protested or taken up diplomatically by India, considering their potential to undermine India’s sovereignty and strategic interests; and
(c) whether Government is monitoring the growing strategic engagement between Pakistan, Bangladesh and China, including collaborative infrastructure projects, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the total funds allocated and utilised under Pradhan Mantri Awaas Yojana- Gramin (PMAY-G) since 2020, State-wise;
(b) the number of houses sanctioned, constructed, and delivered under PMAY-G in Assam since 2020, district-wise;
(c) the manner in which Government is identifying the beneficiaries under PMAY-G given the outdated Census 2011; and
(d) the number of beneficiaries in Assam under PMAY-G who remain without houses due to funding shortages or other constraints?
P

(a) the total amount of domestic and international investment received by all States including Assam in the last five years along with the investment received in current financial year;
(b) the State-wise investment received in public sector for public sector enterprises or Public Private Partnership (PPP) projects and alike in the last five years; 
(b) the district-wise total investment received by Assam during the said period; and
(c) the top five sectors which have received the maximum investment in Assam in the last five years, year-wise?

(a) the number of Multi-Modal Logistics Parks (MMLPs) approved and under construction in the country, along with their locations and expected completion timelines;
(b) the details of the financial allocation and expenditure incurred on MMLPs under the Bharatmala Pariyojana;
(c) the role of private sector participation in the development and operation of MMLPs;
(d) the number of MMLPs planned under Public-Private Partnership (PPP) mode, and the status of their implementation, and; 
(e) whether Government has faced land acquisition challenges or delays in environmental clearances for MMLPs, especially in Assam, if so, the details thereof?
b

(a) the number of prolonged under-trial prisoners identified and released on Constitution Day (November 26, 2024) by Government so far, State-wise;
(b) the criteria used to identify the release of these prolonged under-trial prisoners;
(c) the measures to ensure that they do not face re-incarceration due to systemic delays, if so, the details thereof, and;
(d) whether Government is considering extending this initiative beyond Constitution Day as a regular mechanism to prevent prolonged detention of under-trials, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the current status of the development of National Waterway-16 (NW-16), including the total stretch operational for navigation;
(b) the funds allocated and utilised for the development of NW-16;
(c) the expected timeline for full operationalisation of NW-16;
(d) the steps taken by Government to enhance cargo and passenger movement along this waterway; and 
(e) whether there are any pending environmental or regulatory clearances affecting the progress of NW-16, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the total number of unreserved passengers who travel daily on Indian Railways, along with the details of revenue generated from unreserved ticket sales over the past five years;
(b) whether Government has conducted any study or received complaints regarding overcrowding and lack of basic amenities in general compartments, if so, the details thereof, and; 
(c) whether Government has any plan to introduce more unreserved passenger trains or increase the number of general coaches in existing trains, especially in high-demand routes, if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether the Central Pollution Control Board (CPCB) is a watchdog of State Pollution Control Boards (SPCBs) and Pollution Control Committees (PCCs) and has some regulatory powers, if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether Government has any data on the number of posts laying vacant in the SPCBs and PCCs;
(c) whether Government is taking any steps to ensure timely compliance with the National Green Tribunal's (NGT) directive to fill vacant posts across pollution control boards by April 30, 2025, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the steps taken by CPCB to streamline recruitment processes to address delays in filling vacancies?

(a) the current status of the Silchar-Saurashtra East-West Corridor under the National Highways Development Project (NHDP), including the total length completed so far;
(b) the reasons for the delay in the completion of the project and the steps being taken to expedite the pending work;
(c) the total funds allocated and utilised for the corridor during the last five years;
(d) whether there are any proposed modifications, extensions, or realignments in the project, if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the expected timeline for the full completion of the corridor and its impact on connectivity and economic development?
b

(a) the total seats sanctioned and enroled in graduate courses in medicine, engineering, and management in the last five years, year-wise;
